--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 1: OVERVIEW & CORE ARCHITECTURE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AegisHealth India is an enterprise-grade AI-powered health supply chain and command tower platform built for Primary Healthcare Centres (PHCs) across India (Tamil Nadu, Uttar Pradesh, Assam, Rajasthan). 

Core Capabilities:
1. Real-time GIS Command Control Tower: OpenStreetMap visualization of ~100 PHCs with color-blind accessible non-color shape indicators (triangle for warning, square for critical).
2. Offline Service Worker & IndexedDB Cache: Service worker precaching of app assets + IndexedDB local persistence (`AegisHealthDB`) for stock levels, daily footfall, and offline voice/vision stock updates when connectivity is lost in remote field areas.
3. Multi-Lingual AI Voice Stock Entry: Gemini audio extraction (Hindi, Tamil, Assamese, Bengali, Marathi, English) into structured stock updates.
4. Vision Stock Photo OCR: AI camera image analysis for medicine box counts and stock register logs.
5. Algorithmic Inter-PHC Redistribution Engine: Optimizes stock rebalancing based on transit distance (km), ETA, donor safety buffer, and recipient cover gain.
6. Outbreak & Disaster Scenario Simulator: Stress-tests network against Monsoon Floods, Heatwaves, Snakebite Emergency, and Cholera Outbreaks.
7. Decentralized Federated Learning Monitor: Tracks privacy-preserving state-node model training and WAPE accuracy without centralizing patient raw data.
8. 4 User Login Personas (RBAC):
   - PHC Medical Officer (Frontline)
   - District Health Officer (DHO)
   - State Mission Director (Directorate)
   - National Command Tower (Full Access)
9. Dual Theme Engine:
   - Command Room (High-Contrast Dark Theme)
   - Field Duty / Sunlight Mode (High Outdoor Visibility Light Theme)
10. Sanjeevani AI Copilot: Embedded multi-turn Gemini chatbot grounded on site capabilities, telemetry data, and navigation.

